PostureRMM End-User License Agreement
Last updated: 2026-08-14

Copyright (c) 2026 PostureRMM. All rights reserved.

PostureRMM is proprietary software. It is licensed, not sold. This agreement is
the whole of the permission you have to use it, and it is short on purpose: we
would rather you read it than skim it.


THE SHORT VERSION

  - Run PostureRMM free, forever, on up to 50 endpoints. Every feature.
  - Need more endpoints? Buy an entitlement. It raises the cap. Nothing else
    about the product changes.
  - Manage your own machines, or your customers' machines. Both are fine.
  - Don't redistribute our builds, rebrand them, or defeat the endpoint cap.
  - We give no warranty and we cap our liability. Sections 13 and 14 are the
    two that could cost you. Read those in full.

The short version is a summary, not the agreement. Sections 1 to 17 are.


1. ACCEPTING THIS AGREEMENT

You accept this agreement by downloading, installing, running, or continuing to
use the Software. If you are doing that for an organisation, you are confirming
you have authority to bind it. If you do not accept it, do not install the
Software, and uninstall it if you already have.


2. DEFINITIONS

Software — PostureRMM: the backend, the Bastion, the optional Proxy, the Windows
agent together with its helper and tray components, the installers and container
images we publish, the compliance and posture content bundled with them, and the
documentation shipped alongside. We publish the Software as binaries and
container images only. We do not publish its source code, and nothing in this
agreement grants you any right to source code.

We, us, our — PostureRMM, the publisher of the Software.

You, your — the person or organisation running the Software.

Endpoint — one device, physical or virtual, on which the PostureRMM agent is
installed and enrolled against your installation.

Entitlement — a signed license token we issue to a specific installation,
recording the endpoint cap it is licensed for and the date it is paid through.

Community — the Software running without an Entitlement.

Business — the Software running with a valid Entitlement.

Official Build — a copy of the Software that we published ourselves: a GitHub
Release asset in the official PostureRMM repository, or a container image in a
GitHub Container Registry namespace we control. The README in that repository
lists the current locations.


3. THE LICENSE WE GRANT YOU

Subject to this agreement, we grant you a worldwide, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, royalty-free license to:

  (a) install and run Official Builds of the Software on infrastructure you
      control, in production, across as many separate installations as you
      operate;

  (b) use it to manage endpoints you own, endpoints your organisation operates,
      and endpoints you manage on behalf of your customers. Running PostureRMM
      as a managed service provider is expressly permitted; every endpoint you
      manage counts toward your cap the same as any other;

  (c) make as many copies as you need for backup, staging, testing, and disaster
      recovery, provided those copies stay under this agreement;

  (d) keep running any version you lawfully obtained, for as long as you want to
      run it. We can stop publishing a version; we cannot take back the copy you
      already have.

The right to run the Software is perpetual. An Entitlement does not grant that
right — it raises the endpoint cap for the period it covers (section 5).


4. COMMUNITY: FREE, UP TO 50 ENDPOINTS

Community costs nothing and does not expire. It is the same product as Business,
with the same features: no feature matrix, no surcharge for single sign-on, no
asterisks. The one limit is a cap of 50 endpoints.

Endpoints beyond the cap still enrol, but they sit in a pending state — not
scanned, not scored, not billed — until you have cap for them. The cap is
enforced by the Software in real time. We do not audit you, and there is no
retrospective true-up.


5. BUSINESS: AN ENTITLEMENT RAISES THE CAP

An Entitlement raises your cap to 50 plus the number of seats you purchased. The
first 50 endpoints stay free at any scale. Prices, billing cadence, and payment
terms are the ones stated to you at purchase; they are deliberately not restated
here, so that this file cannot go stale about them.

Two things about how Entitlements behave, because they are promises and not
merely mechanics:

  (a) An Entitlement is valid on your installation until its paid-through date
      plus a seven-day grace period, whether or not that installation can reach
      the internet. Our downtime cannot degrade a paying customer, and a site
      that opens outbound access for one maintenance window a month is a
      first-class customer.

  (b) If an Entitlement lapses, the installation degrades gracefully to
      Community: endpoints beyond 50 move to the pending state, and the first 50
      keep full monitoring. We do not brick installations over a billing event.


6. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

You may not:

  (a) redistribute, publish, mirror, sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or lend
      copies of the Software — binaries, installers, or container images — to
      anyone else. Point them at the Official Builds instead;

  (b) rebrand the Software, or distribute it in whole or in part under another
      name, as your own product, or bundled into another product;

  (c) circumvent, disable, alter, or interfere with the endpoint cap, the
      Entitlement verification, the tier reporting, or any other licensing
      mechanism in the Software; or use an Entitlement that was not issued to
      your installation;

  (d) remove, obscure, or alter our copyright, license, version, or attribution
      notices — in the binaries, in the container images, or in the product's
      own interface;

  (e) reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the Software, or otherwise try
      to derive its source code, except:

        (i)  to the extent applicable law gives you a right to do so that we
             cannot exclude by contract; and

        (ii) for good-faith security research conducted under our vulnerability
             disclosure policy. We would far rather you found a flaw in our
             software than didn't. Report it to security@posturermm.com and we
             will not treat that research as a breach of this section.


7. OFFICIAL BUILDS

This license covers Official Builds only. A copy of PostureRMM obtained anywhere
else — a mirror, a third-party container image, a repackaged installer, a
"patched" build — is not ours. We have not built it, we have not tested it, we
cannot say what is in it, and running it falls outside this agreement.

Take that seriously rather than as legal throat-clearing: a PostureRMM agent
holds administrative control of every machine it is installed on, which makes a
tampered build one of the most valuable things an attacker could hand you.
Official binaries come only from our GitHub Releases. Beware imitations.


8. TRADEMARKS

"PostureRMM", the PostureRMM logo and lockup, and the product's visual identity
are ours. A license to run the Software is not a license to our marks, and
nothing in this agreement grants you one.

You do not need our permission to say, accurately, that you use, run, evaluate,
or provide services on PostureRMM. That is ordinary descriptive use and it is
fine. What is not fine is using our name or marks in a way that suggests we
built, endorsed, or support something we did not, or applying them to a modified
or third-party build.


9. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Software includes third-party components — open-source libraries, fonts, and
icon sets — that remain under their own licenses. Nothing in this agreement
narrows the rights those licenses give you, and where one of them conflicts with
this agreement in respect of that component, that license governs.


10. COMPLIANCE CONTENT IS INFORMATION, NOT CERTIFICATION

PostureRMM measures your endpoints against published benchmarks and public
vulnerability data, and reports what it finds. That is a measurement. It is not
an audit, not a certification, and not legal advice.

A green score is not a statement that you comply with HIPAA, PCI DSS, SOC 2,
ISO 27001, CMMC, Cyber Essentials, or any other framework, and no report the
Software produces substitutes for your own assessment or for an assessor's.
Upstream benchmark and vulnerability data can be incomplete, delayed, or wrong;
we pass on what we are given.


11. YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES

The Software takes administrative control of the endpoints you enrol. It can run
scripts, install and remove software, change security settings, and open a
remote session. That is what an RMM is.

You are responsible for deploying it only on machines you own or are authorised
to manage; for who you grant access to; for the credentials, install keys, and
API tokens you issue; and for keeping your installation patched and reachable
only by people who should reach it. Deploying PostureRMM onto machines you have
no authority over is your act, not ours, and it is a breach of this agreement.


12. WHAT THE SOFTWARE SENDS OUTWARD

The PostureRMM backend makes no outbound internet connections. The Bastion — the
only component that talks to the internet at all — pulls vulnerability,
catalogue, and license data from us on a schedule you control.

Riding that pull is a single usage record: installation ID, product version,
tier, and endpoint count. That is the whole of it. Your fleet data, your
inventory, your scan results, your compliance findings, and your endpoints'
identities stay on your own infrastructure. We do not collect them, and the
architecture gives us no route to.


13. NO WARRANTY

As far as the law allows, the Software is provided as it is, with no warranty or
condition of any kind, express or implied — including any implied warranty of
merchantability, satisfactory quality, fitness for a particular purpose,
accuracy, title, or non-infringement.

We do not warrant that the Software will be uninterrupted, error-free, or
secure; that it will detect every vulnerability, misconfiguration, or fault on
your endpoints; or that anything it reports is correct or complete. You decide
whether to run it, and you are responsible for judging whether it is fit for
what you need it to do.


14. LIMITS ON LIABILITY

As far as the law allows:

  (a) we are not liable to you for any indirect, incidental, special,
      consequential, or punitive damages, nor for lost profits, lost revenue,
      lost or corrupted data, business interruption, or the cost of substitute
      software or services, arising out of or relating to the Software or this
      agreement, under any legal theory, even if we were told such damages were
      possible; and

  (b) our total liability to you for everything arising out of or relating to
      the Software or this agreement is capped at the greater of (i) the amounts
      you paid us for Entitlements in the twelve months before the claim arose,
      and (ii) one hundred United States dollars. If you run Community you have
      paid us nothing, and the cap is one hundred United States dollars.

This is a deliberate allocation of risk, and it is part of why the Software
costs what it costs: a free tier and a one-dollar-per-endpoint price cannot
carry unbounded liability.

Nothing in this agreement excludes or limits any liability that cannot lawfully
be excluded or limited — including liability for death or personal injury caused
by negligence, and liability for fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation. Some
jurisdictions do not allow some of the exclusions above; where that is so, they
apply to you only as far as that jurisdiction allows.


15. TERM, TERMINATION, AND WHAT SURVIVES

This agreement starts when you accept it and runs until it ends.

You may end it at any time, by uninstalling the Software.

We may end it if you materially breach section 6 (What you may not do) or
section 11 (Your responsibilities) and do not fix the breach within 30 days of
us telling you about it in writing. Where a breach cannot sensibly be
fixed — you have published our builds under another name, say — it ends when we
tell you.

When it ends, stop using the Software and delete every copy you hold, including
container images. Termination for breach does not entitle you to a refund of any
Entitlement.

We have no remote kill switch, and this agreement does not give us one. Nothing
here lets us reach into your installation and disable it; our only lever is
declining to issue or renew an Entitlement. Termination is a legal event, not a
technical one.

Sections 2, 8, 9, 10, 13, 14, 16, and 17 survive termination, together with any
payment obligation that had already accrued.


16. GENERAL

Which version applies. The version of this agreement that shipped with your copy
of the Software governs that copy. We may change the terms for later releases;
doing so never changes the terms of a release you already have.

Severability. If a court finds part of this agreement unenforceable, the rest
stays in force, and the unenforceable part is narrowed to what is enforceable.

No waiver. If we do not enforce something immediately, we have not given it up.

Entire agreement. This is the whole agreement about the Software between you and
us, and it replaces anything said before. Where a written order form or purchase
agreement signed by both of us conflicts with it, that document governs.

Assignment. You may not transfer this agreement or an Entitlement without our
written consent, except to a successor of your entire business. We may assign
this agreement.


17. GOVERNING LAW

This agreement is governed by the laws of the Isle of Man, without regard to its
conflict-of-law rules, and the courts of the Isle of Man have exclusive
jurisdiction over any dispute arising out of or relating to it. The United
Nations Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods does not
apply.

Nothing in this section takes away a right you have under the mandatory consumer
law of the country you live in, where that law says it cannot be excluded by
agreement.


